{"root":{"children":[{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"What is Boulder Colorado Voter Guide?","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"extended-heading","version":1,"tag":"h2"},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Eric Budd runs the Boulder Colorado Voter Guide, a blog where he shares his personal endorsements and research for local elections. He has published these guides for every Boulder election for ten years. Boulder Colorado Voter Guide is a comprehensive, general-purpose, well-researched and sourced ","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"voter guide for the 2025 election in Boulder, Colorado","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"link","version":1,"rel":"noreferrer","target":null,"title":null,"url":"https://bouldercoloradovoterguide.com/election-guide"},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":".","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Why is Eric Budd a good source of information for the Boulder election?","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"extended-heading","version":1,"tag":"h2"},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Eric Budd’s voter guide is influential locally and is well known among Boulder’s politically engaged community. Eric has been a ","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"community organizer","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"link","version":1,"rel":"noreferrer","target":null,"title":null,"url":"https://bouldercoloradovoterguide.com/about-eric-budd/"},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":" in Boulder for more than ten years and notes his affiliations with Boulder Progressives, Better Boulder, and as a lead on local ballot measure campaigns. His guides reflect a progressive perspective but include over 100 sources and links so that readers can research and come to their own conclusions.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Key aspects of Eric Budd’s Boulder Colorado Voter Guide:","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"extended-heading","version":1,"tag":"h3"},{"children":[{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Focuses on local elections:","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":" While Eric occasionally weighs in on statewide or national issues, the primary purpose of the blog is to provide recommendations for local issues, candidates, and ballot measures in Boulder.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"listitem","version":1,"value":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Progressive viewpoint:","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":" Eric’s guides consistently reflect his progressive political stance. He uses them to advocate for candidates and issues that align with his views on housing, social justice, and climate action. For example, he has used the blog to justify his vote on issues like raising occupancy limits and moving municipal elections.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"listitem","version":1,"value":2},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"References to local reporting:","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":" Budd’s voter guides often reference reporting from local journalists and news outlets, such as Boulder Reporting Lab, The Daily Camera, Shay Castle, Richard Valenty, or others. This helps to ground his opinions in local context, but his analyses are ultimately his own.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"listitem","version":1,"value":3},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Blog format and availability:","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":" The voter guide is published on a blog, bouldercoloradovoterguide.com. This makes it widely accessible and shareable online. He has also used social media, like Bluesky, to promote his most recent guides.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"listitem","version":1,"value":4},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Community resource:","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":" The guide has served as a resource for many local voters seeking a progressive perspective on Boulder elections. He relies on local reporting and research to formulate his opinions and endorsements.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"listitem","version":1,"value":5}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"list","version":1,"listType":"bullet","start":1,"tag":"ul"},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Which candidates did Boulder Colorado Voter Guide support for Boulder City Council?","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"extended-heading","version":1,"tag":"h2"},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Boulder Colorado Voter Guide supports five candidates for Boulder City Council in 2026:","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Ryan Schuchard","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"link","version":1,"rel":"noreferrer noopener","target":"_blank","title":null,"url":"https://www.ryanwithboulder.com/"}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"listitem","version":1,"value":1},{"children":[{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Jamillah Richmond","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"link","version":1,"rel":"noreferrer noopener","target":"_blank","title":null,"url":"http://jamillahanewvoice.com/"}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"listitem","version":1,"value":2},{"children":[{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Sam Fuqua","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"link","version":1,"rel":"noreferrer noopener","target":"_blank","title":null,"url":"https://www.fuquaforcouncil.com/"}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"listitem","version":1,"value":3},{"children":[{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Jill Adler Grano","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"link","version":1,"rel":"noreferrer noopener","target":"_blank","title":null,"url":"https://www.jillforcouncil.com/"}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"listitem","version":1,"value":4},{"children":[{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Tina Marquis","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"link","version":1,"rel":"noreferrer noopener","target":"_blank","title":null,"url":"https://www.tinaforbou